---
title: Custom Events Reference
id: custom-events
order: 1
description: "Every CUSTOM event TanStack AI itself emits, unified as KnownCustomEvent, and the ChatStream type that lets a plain `if (chunk.name === '…')` narrow chunk.value — no helper, no cast."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - custom events
  - KnownCustomEvent
  - ChatStream
  - ag-ui protocol
  - CUSTOM event
  - stream narrowing
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You're reading a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" stream and you've hit a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" event — maybe\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/events","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox.file.diff"}]},{"type":"text","value":", maybe a Code Mode progress event,\nmaybe "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.complete"},{"type":"text","value":". Each feature page documents its own\nevents in context. This page is the map: every "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" event TanStack AI\nitself emits, in one table, plus the type mechanism that lets you read any of\nthem with a plain "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"if"},{"type":"text","value":" — no helper function, no cast."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-type-chatstream","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatStream"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatStream"},{"type":"text","value":" by default (no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stream"},{"type":"text","value":" not\nexplicitly "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":"):"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport type { ChatStream } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst stream: ChatStream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n});","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatStream"},{"type":"text","value":" is defined as:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type ChatStream = AsyncIterable<Exclude<StreamChunk, CustomEvent> | KnownCustomEvent>","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StreamChunk"},{"type":"text","value":" (the raw AG-UI event union) has exactly one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":"-shaped\nmember: the generic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" interface, with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name: string"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value: any"},{"type":"text","value":". Left in the union unchanged, that single "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":" \"poisons\" every\nnarrow — even "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"if (chunk.type === 'CUSTOM' && chunk.name === 'sandbox.file')"},{"type":"text","value":"\nwould still leave "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.value"},{"type":"text","value":" typed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":", because TypeScript can't\ndistinguish the generic member from a specific one once they're merged.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatStream"},{"type":"text","value":" fixes this in two steps: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Exclude<StreamChunk, CustomEvent>"},{"type":"text","value":"\nremoves that generic member, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"| KnownCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" adds back a\ndiscriminated union of every event TanStack AI actually emits — each with a\nliteral "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" and a concrete "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":". The result is a stream where "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":"\nevents narrow like anything else."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reading-events-the-plain-narrowing-pattern","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reading events: the plain narrowing pattern"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.type === 'CUSTOM'"},{"type":"text","value":", then compare "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.name"},{"type":"text","value":" to a literal\nstring. That's the entire client-side API — there is no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isSandboxEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" guard to import:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n});\n\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"sandbox.file.diff\") {\n    console.log(chunk.value.path, chunk.value.diff); // typed, no helper, no cast\n  } else if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"structured-output.complete\") {\n    console.log(chunk.value.object); // typed, no helper, no cast\n  }\n}","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"full-taxonomy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full taxonomy"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every interface below extends the base "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"type: 'CUSTOM'"},{"type":"text","value":", plus\nan optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model?"},{"type":"text","value":") with a literal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" and a concrete "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":". All are\nunioned as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"KnownCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":", exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai"},{"type":"text","value":" alongside each\nindividual interface."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interface"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Emitted when"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SandboxFileCustomEvent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox.file"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type: 'create' | 'change' | 'delete'; path: string; timestamp: number }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"per file create/change/delete in an active "},{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/events","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sandbox"}]}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SandboxFileDiffEvent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox.file.diff"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ path: string; diff: string }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"per file change, opt-in via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fileEvents: { diff: true }"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FileChangedEvent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file.changed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ path: string; diff: string }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a harness adapter (Grok Build, Claude Code, …), once after the run completes"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SessionIdEvent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"`${string}.session-id`"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ sessionId: string }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a harness adapter, once when its in-sandbox session is created or resumed"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CodeModeExecutionStartedEvent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:execution_started"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ timestamp: number; codeLength: number }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../code-mode/code-mode","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Mode"}]},{"type":"text","value":", when sandbox execution begins"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CodeModeConsoleEvent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:console"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ level: 'log' | 'warn' | 'error' | 'info'; message: string; timestamp: number }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Mode, per "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"console.*"},{"type":"text","value":" call inside the sandbox"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CodeModeExternalCallEvent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:external_call"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ function: string; args: unknown; timestamp: number }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Mode, before a bound "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"external_*"},{"type":"text","value":" function runs"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CodeModeExternalResultEvent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:external_result"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ function: string; result: unknown; duration: number }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Mode, after a successful "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"external_*"},{"type":"text","value":" call"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CodeModeExternalErrorEvent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:external_error"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ function: string; error: string; duration: number }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Mode, when an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"external_*"},{"type":"text","value":" call throws"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CodeModeSnippetCallEvent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:snippet_call"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ snippet: string; input: unknown; timestamp: number }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../code-mode/code-mode-with-snippets","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Mode with Snippets"}]},{"type":"text","value":", before a snippet runs"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CodeModeSnippetResultEvent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:snippet_result"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ snippet: string; result: unknown; duration: number; timestamp: number }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Mode with Snippets, after a successful snippet run"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CodeModeSnippetErrorEvent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:snippet_error"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ snippet: string; error: string; duration: number; timestamp: number }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Mode with Snippets, when a snippet throws"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SnippetRegisteredEvent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snippet:registered"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ id: string; name: string; description: string; timestamp: number }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"when a snippet is registered into the tool registry"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StructuredOutputStartEvent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.start"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ messageId: string }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../structured-outputs/streaming","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ outputSchema, stream: true })"}]},{"type":"text","value":", once per structured message"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StructuredOutputCompleteEvent<T>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.complete"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ object: T; raw: string; reasoning?: string }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"structured-output streaming, once with the validated object"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ApprovalRequestedEvent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"approval-requested"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ toolCallId: string; toolName: string; input: unknown; approval: { id: string; needsApproval: true } }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a server tool needs approval — the run pauses; see "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/tool-approval","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool Approval Flow"}]}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolInputAvailableEvent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool-input-available"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ toolCallId: string; toolName: string; input: unknown }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a client tool is invoked — the run pauses; see "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/client-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client Tools"}]}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UIResourceEvent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ui-resource"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ resource; serverId?: string; toolCallId: string; toolName: string; meta?: Record<string, unknown> }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"an MCP tool returns a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ui://"},{"type":"text","value":" resource ("},{"type":"link","href":"../mcp/apps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MCP Apps"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"these-stay-custom","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These stay CUSTOM"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*.session-id"},{"type":"text","value":" events and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.start"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.complete"},{"type":"text","value":" stay "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":". They are not fields on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read them with the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"...\""},{"type":"text","value":" branch as the rest of this page. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../structured-outputs/streaming","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming structured output"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the complete event."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"your-own-custom-events-aren-t-in-this-union","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your own custom events aren't in this union"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools and chat middleware can emit application-defined events through\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"emitCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A server tool receives "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"emitCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" on its execution context:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst importRows = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"importRows\",\n  description: \"Import rows into the dataset, reporting progress as it runs\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ rows: z.array(z.string()) }),\n}).server(async ({ rows }, context) => {\n  for (let i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {\n    context?.emitCustomEvent(\"my-app:progress\", {\n      done: i + 1,\n      total: rows.length,\n    });\n  }\n  return { imported: rows.length };\n});","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chat middleware calls the same helper on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatMiddlewareContext"},{"type":"text","value":". The engine\nyields the chunk while the hook is still running, so a long "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" can\nsend "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"started"},{"type":"text","value":" before the work finishes:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nasync function prepare() {\n  await new Promise<void>((resolve) => {\n    setTimeout(resolve, 1);\n  });\n}\n\nconst progress: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"progress\",\n  async onConfig(ctx) {\n    if (ctx.phase !== \"beforeModel\") return;\n    ctx.emitCustomEvent(\"my-app:progress\", { step: \"prepare\" });\n    await prepare();\n    ctx.emitCustomEvent(\"my-app:progress\", { step: \"ready\" });\n  },\n};","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With durability on the response, each of these events flushes as soon as it\nis emitted, so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prepare"},{"type":"text","value":" reaches the client while "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prepare()"},{"type":"text","value":" is still\nrunning. High-volume names stay in the durability batch:\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"process.stdout"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"process.stderr"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox.file"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox.file.diff"},{"type":"text","value":".\nPass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ batch: true }"},{"type":"text","value":" to keep one of your own events in that batch:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst noisy: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"noisy\",\n  async onConfig(ctx) {\n    ctx.emitCustomEvent(\"my-app:ticks\", { n: 1 }, { batch: true });\n  },\n};","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These flow over the wire exactly like the built-in events: same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":"\nchunk shape, same runtime behavior. But "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'my-app:progress'"},{"type":"text","value":" isn't one of the\nliteral names in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"KnownCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":", so it's intentionally absent from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatStream"},{"type":"text","value":"'s type. This is the same tradeoff "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StructuredOutputStream"},{"type":"text","value":"\nalready made: including a generic fallback member would reintroduce the\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value: any"},{"type":"text","value":" poison for every other event on the stream."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To read your own event's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":", don't rely on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatStream"},{"type":"text","value":"'s narrowed\nunion for that branch — annotate the stream as the wider "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StreamChunk"},{"type":"text","value":" type\ninstead, where the generic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" member's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value: any"},{"type":"text","value":" needs no cast:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport type { StreamChunk } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { importRows } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst stream: AsyncIterable<StreamChunk> = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Import these rows\" }],\n  tools: [importRows],\n});\n\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"my-app:progress\") {\n    console.log(chunk.value.done, chunk.value.total); // value: any — your event, your shape\n  }\n}","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The event still arrives at runtime either way — this only changes what\nTypeScript will let you write. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatStream"},{"type":"text","value":" is the right default for reading\nTanStack AI's own events with full type safety; fall back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StreamChunk"},{"type":"text","value":"\nfor the branches that read your own."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"related","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Related"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./metadata","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Event metadata"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.tanstack"},{"type":"text","value":" fields a custom AG-UI server must send so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" gets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"finishReason"},{"type":"text","value":" and model."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/events","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sandbox Events"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — the sandbox- and harness-specific rows of this table, in context, plus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox.file.diff"},{"type":"text","value":"'s opt-in."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/observability","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Observability"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — the server-side hook accessors ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"before()"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"after()"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"diff()"},{"type":"text","value":") that back "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox.file.diff"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../code-mode/client-integration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Showing Code Mode in the UI"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — rendering the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:*"},{"type":"text","value":" events live."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../structured-outputs/streaming","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming UIs"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — reading "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.complete"},{"type":"text","value":" end to end."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../chat/stream-events","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stream Events"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the standard AG-UI "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StreamChunk"},{"type":"text","value":" lifecycle this union extends."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"the-type-chatstream","text":"The type: ChatStream","level":2},{"id":"reading-events-the-plain-narrowing-pattern","text":"Reading events: the plain narrowing pattern","level":2},{"id":"full-taxonomy","text":"Full taxonomy","level":2},{"id":"these-stay-custom","text":"These stay CUSTOM","level":2},{"id":"your-own-custom-events-aren-t-in-this-union","text":"Your own custom events aren't in this union","level":2},{"id":"related","text":"Related","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou're reading a `chat()` stream and you've hit a `CUSTOM` event — maybe\n[`sandbox.file.diff`](../sandbox/events), maybe a Code Mode progress event,\nmaybe `structured-output.complete`. Each feature page documents its own\nevents in context. This page is the map: every `CUSTOM` event TanStack AI\nitself emits, in one table, plus the type mechanism that lets you read any of\nthem with a plain `if` — no helper function, no cast.\n\n## The type: `ChatStream`\n\n`chat()` returns `ChatStream` by default (no `outputSchema`, `stream` not\nexplicitly `false`):\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport type { ChatStream } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst stream: ChatStream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n});\n```\n\n`ChatStream` is defined as:\n\n```ts ignore\ntype ChatStream = AsyncIterable<Exclude<StreamChunk, CustomEvent> | KnownCustomEvent>\n```\n\n`StreamChunk` (the raw AG-UI event union) has exactly one `CUSTOM`-shaped\nmember: the generic `CustomEvent` interface, with `name: string` and\n`value: any`. Left in the union unchanged, that single `any` \"poisons\" every\nnarrow — even `if (chunk.type === 'CUSTOM' && chunk.name === 'sandbox.file')`\nwould still leave `chunk.value` typed `any`, because TypeScript can't\ndistinguish the generic member from a specific one once they're merged.\n`ChatStream` fixes this in two steps: `Exclude<StreamChunk, CustomEvent>`\nremoves that generic member, and `| KnownCustomEvent` adds back a\ndiscriminated union of every event TanStack AI actually emits — each with a\nliteral `name` and a concrete `value`. The result is a stream where `CUSTOM`\nevents narrow like anything else.\n\n## Reading events: the plain narrowing pattern\n\nCheck `chunk.type === 'CUSTOM'`, then compare `chunk.name` to a literal\nstring. That's the entire client-side API — there is no `isCustomEvent` or\n`isSandboxEvent` guard to import:\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n});\n\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"sandbox.file.diff\") {\n    console.log(chunk.value.path, chunk.value.diff); // typed, no helper, no cast\n  } else if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"structured-output.complete\") {\n    console.log(chunk.value.object); // typed, no helper, no cast\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Full taxonomy\n\nEvery interface below extends the base `CustomEvent` (`type: 'CUSTOM'`, plus\nan optional `model?`) with a literal `name` and a concrete `value`. All are\nunioned as `KnownCustomEvent`, exported from `@tanstack/ai` alongside each\nindividual interface.\n\n| Interface | `name` | `value` | Emitted when |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `SandboxFileCustomEvent` | `sandbox.file` | `{ type: 'create' \\| 'change' \\| 'delete'; path: string; timestamp: number }` | per file create/change/delete in an active [sandbox](../sandbox/events) |\n| `SandboxFileDiffEvent` | `sandbox.file.diff` | `{ path: string; diff: string }` | per file change, opt-in via `fileEvents: { diff: true }` |\n| `FileChangedEvent` | `file.changed` | `{ path: string; diff: string }` | a harness adapter (Grok Build, Claude Code, …), once after the run completes |\n| `SessionIdEvent` | `` `${string}.session-id` `` | `{ sessionId: string }` | a harness adapter, once when its in-sandbox session is created or resumed |\n| `CodeModeExecutionStartedEvent` | `code_mode:execution_started` | `{ timestamp: number; codeLength: number }` | [Code Mode](../code-mode/code-mode), when sandbox execution begins |\n| `CodeModeConsoleEvent` | `code_mode:console` | `{ level: 'log' \\| 'warn' \\| 'error' \\| 'info'; message: string; timestamp: number }` | Code Mode, per `console.*` call inside the sandbox |\n| `CodeModeExternalCallEvent` | `code_mode:external_call` | `{ function: string; args: unknown; timestamp: number }` | Code Mode, before a bound `external_*` function runs |\n| `CodeModeExternalResultEvent` | `code_mode:external_result` | `{ function: string; result: unknown; duration: number }` | Code Mode, after a successful `external_*` call |\n| `CodeModeExternalErrorEvent` | `code_mode:external_error` | `{ function: string; error: string; duration: number }` | Code Mode, when an `external_*` call throws |\n| `CodeModeSnippetCallEvent` | `code_mode:snippet_call` | `{ snippet: string; input: unknown; timestamp: number }` | [Code Mode with Snippets](../code-mode/code-mode-with-snippets), before a snippet runs |\n| `CodeModeSnippetResultEvent` | `code_mode:snippet_result` | `{ snippet: string; result: unknown; duration: number; timestamp: number }` | Code Mode with Snippets, after a successful snippet run |\n| `CodeModeSnippetErrorEvent` | `code_mode:snippet_error` | `{ snippet: string; error: string; duration: number; timestamp: number }` | Code Mode with Snippets, when a snippet throws |\n| `SnippetRegisteredEvent` | `snippet:registered` | `{ id: string; name: string; description: string; timestamp: number }` | when a snippet is registered into the tool registry |\n| `StructuredOutputStartEvent` | `structured-output.start` | `{ messageId: string }` | [`chat({ outputSchema, stream: true })`](../structured-outputs/streaming), once per structured message |\n| `StructuredOutputCompleteEvent<T>` | `structured-output.complete` | `{ object: T; raw: string; reasoning?: string }` | structured-output streaming, once with the validated object |\n| `ApprovalRequestedEvent` | `approval-requested` | `{ toolCallId: string; toolName: string; input: unknown; approval: { id: string; needsApproval: true } }` | a server tool needs approval — the run pauses; see [Tool Approval Flow](../tools/tool-approval) |\n| `ToolInputAvailableEvent` | `tool-input-available` | `{ toolCallId: string; toolName: string; input: unknown }` | a client tool is invoked — the run pauses; see [Client Tools](../tools/client-tools) |\n| `UIResourceEvent` | `ui-resource` | `{ resource; serverId?: string; toolCallId: string; toolName: string; meta?: Record<string, unknown> }` | an MCP tool returns a `ui://` resource ([MCP Apps](../mcp/apps)) |\n\n## These stay CUSTOM\n\nHarness `*.session-id` events and `structured-output.start` / `structured-output.complete` stay `CUSTOM`. They are not fields on `RUN_FINISHED`.\n\nRead them with the same `chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"...\"` branch as the rest of this page. See [Streaming structured output](../structured-outputs/streaming) for the complete event.\n\n## Your own custom events aren't in this union\n\nTools and chat middleware can emit application-defined events through\n`emitCustomEvent`.\n\nA server tool receives `emitCustomEvent` on its execution context:\n\n```ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst importRows = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"importRows\",\n  description: \"Import rows into the dataset, reporting progress as it runs\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ rows: z.array(z.string()) }),\n}).server(async ({ rows }, context) => {\n  for (let i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {\n    context?.emitCustomEvent(\"my-app:progress\", {\n      done: i + 1,\n      total: rows.length,\n    });\n  }\n  return { imported: rows.length };\n});\n```\n\nChat middleware calls the same helper on `ChatMiddlewareContext`. The engine\nyields the chunk while the hook is still running, so a long `onConfig` can\nsend `started` before the work finishes:\n\n```ts\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nasync function prepare() {\n  await new Promise<void>((resolve) => {\n    setTimeout(resolve, 1);\n  });\n}\n\nconst progress: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"progress\",\n  async onConfig(ctx) {\n    if (ctx.phase !== \"beforeModel\") return;\n    ctx.emitCustomEvent(\"my-app:progress\", { step: \"prepare\" });\n    await prepare();\n    ctx.emitCustomEvent(\"my-app:progress\", { step: \"ready\" });\n  },\n};\n```\n\nWith durability on the response, each of these events flushes as soon as it\nis emitted, so `prepare` reaches the client while `prepare()` is still\nrunning. High-volume names stay in the durability batch:\n`process.stdout`, `process.stderr`, `sandbox.file`, and `sandbox.file.diff`.\nPass `{ batch: true }` to keep one of your own events in that batch:\n\n```ts\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst noisy: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"noisy\",\n  async onConfig(ctx) {\n    ctx.emitCustomEvent(\"my-app:ticks\", { n: 1 }, { batch: true });\n  },\n};\n```\n\nThese flow over the wire exactly like the built-in events: same `CUSTOM`\nchunk shape, same runtime behavior. But `'my-app:progress'` isn't one of the\nliteral names in `KnownCustomEvent`, so it's intentionally absent from\n`ChatStream`'s type. This is the same tradeoff `StructuredOutputStream`\nalready made: including a generic fallback member would reintroduce the\n`value: any` poison for every other event on the stream.\n\nTo read your own event's `value`, don't rely on `ChatStream`'s narrowed\nunion for that branch — annotate the stream as the wider `StreamChunk` type\ninstead, where the generic `CUSTOM` member's `value: any` needs no cast:\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport type { StreamChunk } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { importRows } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst stream: AsyncIterable<StreamChunk> = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Import these rows\" }],\n  tools: [importRows],\n});\n\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"my-app:progress\") {\n    console.log(chunk.value.done, chunk.value.total); // value: any — your event, your shape\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe event still arrives at runtime either way — this only changes what\nTypeScript will let you write. `ChatStream` is the right default for reading\nTanStack AI's own events with full type safety; fall back to `StreamChunk`\nfor the branches that read your own.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Event metadata](./metadata) — `metadata.tanstack` fields a custom AG-UI server must send so `useChat` gets `finishReason` and model.\n- [Sandbox Events](../sandbox/events) — the sandbox- and harness-specific rows of this table, in context, plus `sandbox.file.diff`'s opt-in.\n- [Observability](../sandbox/observability) — the server-side hook accessors (`before()`/`after()`/`diff()`) that back `sandbox.file.diff`.\n- [Showing Code Mode in the UI](../code-mode/client-integration) — rendering the `code_mode:*` events live.\n- [Streaming UIs](../structured-outputs/streaming) — reading `structured-output.complete` end to end.\n- [Stream Events](../chat/stream-events) for the standard AG-UI `StreamChunk` lifecycle this union extends.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Custom Events Reference\nid: custom-events\norder: 1\ndescription: \"Every CUSTOM event TanStack AI itself emits, unified as KnownCustomEvent, and the ChatStream type that lets a plain `if (chunk.name === '…')` narrow chunk.value — no helper, no cast.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - custom events\n  - KnownCustomEvent\n  - ChatStream\n  - ag-ui protocol\n  - CUSTOM event\n  - stream narrowing\n---\n\nYou're reading a `chat()` stream and you've hit a `CUSTOM` event — maybe\n[`sandbox.file.diff`](../sandbox/events), maybe a Code Mode progress event,\nmaybe `structured-output.complete`. Each feature page documents its own\nevents in context. This page is the map: every `CUSTOM` event TanStack AI\nitself emits, in one table, plus the type mechanism that lets you read any of\nthem with a plain `if` — no helper function, no cast.\n\n## The type: `ChatStream`\n\n`chat()` returns `ChatStream` by default (no `outputSchema`, `stream` not\nexplicitly `false`):\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport type { ChatStream } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst stream: ChatStream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n});\n```\n\n`ChatStream` is defined as:\n\n```ts ignore\ntype ChatStream = AsyncIterable<Exclude<StreamChunk, CustomEvent> | KnownCustomEvent>\n```\n\n`StreamChunk` (the raw AG-UI event union) has exactly one `CUSTOM`-shaped\nmember: the generic `CustomEvent` interface, with `name: string` and\n`value: any`. Left in the union unchanged, that single `any` \"poisons\" every\nnarrow — even `if (chunk.type === 'CUSTOM' && chunk.name === 'sandbox.file')`\nwould still leave `chunk.value` typed `any`, because TypeScript can't\ndistinguish the generic member from a specific one once they're merged.\n`ChatStream` fixes this in two steps: `Exclude<StreamChunk, CustomEvent>`\nremoves that generic member, and `| KnownCustomEvent` adds back a\ndiscriminated union of every event TanStack AI actually emits — each with a\nliteral `name` and a concrete `value`. The result is a stream where `CUSTOM`\nevents narrow like anything else.\n\n## Reading events: the plain narrowing pattern\n\nCheck `chunk.type === 'CUSTOM'`, then compare `chunk.name` to a literal\nstring. That's the entire client-side API — there is no `isCustomEvent` or\n`isSandboxEvent` guard to import:\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n});\n\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"sandbox.file.diff\") {\n    console.log(chunk.value.path, chunk.value.diff); // typed, no helper, no cast\n  } else if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"structured-output.complete\") {\n    console.log(chunk.value.object); // typed, no helper, no cast\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Full taxonomy\n\nEvery interface below extends the base `CustomEvent` (`type: 'CUSTOM'`, plus\nan optional `model?`) with a literal `name` and a concrete `value`. All are\nunioned as `KnownCustomEvent`, exported from `@tanstack/ai` alongside each\nindividual interface.\n\n| Interface | `name` | `value` | Emitted when |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `SandboxFileCustomEvent` | `sandbox.file` | `{ type: 'create' \\| 'change' \\| 'delete'; path: string; timestamp: number }` | per file create/change/delete in an active [sandbox](../sandbox/events) |\n| `SandboxFileDiffEvent` | `sandbox.file.diff` | `{ path: string; diff: string }` | per file change, opt-in via `fileEvents: { diff: true }` |\n| `FileChangedEvent` | `file.changed` | `{ path: string; diff: string }` | a harness adapter (Grok Build, Claude Code, …), once after the run completes |\n| `SessionIdEvent` | `` `${string}.session-id` `` | `{ sessionId: string }` | a harness adapter, once when its in-sandbox session is created or resumed |\n| `CodeModeExecutionStartedEvent` | `code_mode:execution_started` | `{ timestamp: number; codeLength: number }` | [Code Mode](../code-mode/code-mode), when sandbox execution begins |\n| `CodeModeConsoleEvent` | `code_mode:console` | `{ level: 'log' \\| 'warn' \\| 'error' \\| 'info'; message: string; timestamp: number }` | Code Mode, per `console.*` call inside the sandbox |\n| `CodeModeExternalCallEvent` | `code_mode:external_call` | `{ function: string; args: unknown; timestamp: number }` | Code Mode, before a bound `external_*` function runs |\n| `CodeModeExternalResultEvent` | `code_mode:external_result` | `{ function: string; result: unknown; duration: number }` | Code Mode, after a successful `external_*` call |\n| `CodeModeExternalErrorEvent` | `code_mode:external_error` | `{ function: string; error: string; duration: number }` | Code Mode, when an `external_*` call throws |\n| `CodeModeSnippetCallEvent` | `code_mode:snippet_call` | `{ snippet: string; input: unknown; timestamp: number }` | [Code Mode with Snippets](../code-mode/code-mode-with-snippets), before a snippet runs |\n| `CodeModeSnippetResultEvent` | `code_mode:snippet_result` | `{ snippet: string; result: unknown; duration: number; timestamp: number }` | Code Mode with Snippets, after a successful snippet run |\n| `CodeModeSnippetErrorEvent` | `code_mode:snippet_error` | `{ snippet: string; error: string; duration: number; timestamp: number }` | Code Mode with Snippets, when a snippet throws |\n| `SnippetRegisteredEvent` | `snippet:registered` | `{ id: string; name: string; description: string; timestamp: number }` | when a snippet is registered into the tool registry |\n| `StructuredOutputStartEvent` | `structured-output.start` | `{ messageId: string }` | [`chat({ outputSchema, stream: true })`](../structured-outputs/streaming), once per structured message |\n| `StructuredOutputCompleteEvent<T>` | `structured-output.complete` | `{ object: T; raw: string; reasoning?: string }` | structured-output streaming, once with the validated object |\n| `ApprovalRequestedEvent` | `approval-requested` | `{ toolCallId: string; toolName: string; input: unknown; approval: { id: string; needsApproval: true } }` | a server tool needs approval — the run pauses; see [Tool Approval Flow](../tools/tool-approval) |\n| `ToolInputAvailableEvent` | `tool-input-available` | `{ toolCallId: string; toolName: string; input: unknown }` | a client tool is invoked — the run pauses; see [Client Tools](../tools/client-tools) |\n| `UIResourceEvent` | `ui-resource` | `{ resource; serverId?: string; toolCallId: string; toolName: string; meta?: Record<string, unknown> }` | an MCP tool returns a `ui://` resource ([MCP Apps](../mcp/apps)) |\n\n## These stay CUSTOM\n\nHarness `*.session-id` events and `structured-output.start` / `structured-output.complete` stay `CUSTOM`. They are not fields on `RUN_FINISHED`.\n\nRead them with the same `chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"...\"` branch as the rest of this page. See [Streaming structured output](../structured-outputs/streaming) for the complete event.\n\n## Your own custom events aren't in this union\n\nTools and chat middleware can emit application-defined events through\n`emitCustomEvent`.\n\nA server tool receives `emitCustomEvent` on its execution context:\n\n```ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst importRows = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"importRows\",\n  description: \"Import rows into the dataset, reporting progress as it runs\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ rows: z.array(z.string()) }),\n}).server(async ({ rows }, context) => {\n  for (let i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {\n    context?.emitCustomEvent(\"my-app:progress\", {\n      done: i + 1,\n      total: rows.length,\n    });\n  }\n  return { imported: rows.length };\n});\n```\n\nChat middleware calls the same helper on `ChatMiddlewareContext`. The engine\nyields the chunk while the hook is still running, so a long `onConfig` can\nsend `started` before the work finishes:\n\n```ts\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nasync function prepare() {\n  await new Promise<void>((resolve) => {\n    setTimeout(resolve, 1);\n  });\n}\n\nconst progress: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"progress\",\n  async onConfig(ctx) {\n    if (ctx.phase !== \"beforeModel\") return;\n    ctx.emitCustomEvent(\"my-app:progress\", { step: \"prepare\" });\n    await prepare();\n    ctx.emitCustomEvent(\"my-app:progress\", { step: \"ready\" });\n  },\n};\n```\n\nWith durability on the response, each of these events flushes as soon as it\nis emitted, so `prepare` reaches the client while `prepare()` is still\nrunning. High-volume names stay in the durability batch:\n`process.stdout`, `process.stderr`, `sandbox.file`, and `sandbox.file.diff`.\nPass `{ batch: true }` to keep one of your own events in that batch:\n\n```ts\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nconst noisy: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: \"noisy\",\n  async onConfig(ctx) {\n    ctx.emitCustomEvent(\"my-app:ticks\", { n: 1 }, { batch: true });\n  },\n};\n```\n\nThese flow over the wire exactly like the built-in events: same `CUSTOM`\nchunk shape, same runtime behavior. But `'my-app:progress'` isn't one of the\nliteral names in `KnownCustomEvent`, so it's intentionally absent from\n`ChatStream`'s type. This is the same tradeoff `StructuredOutputStream`\nalready made: including a generic fallback member would reintroduce the\n`value: any` poison for every other event on the stream.\n\nTo read your own event's `value`, don't rely on `ChatStream`'s narrowed\nunion for that branch — annotate the stream as the wider `StreamChunk` type\ninstead, where the generic `CUSTOM` member's `value: any` needs no cast:\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport type { StreamChunk } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { importRows } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst stream: AsyncIterable<StreamChunk> = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Import these rows\" }],\n  tools: [importRows],\n});\n\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"my-app:progress\") {\n    console.log(chunk.value.done, chunk.value.total); // value: any — your event, your shape\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe event still arrives at runtime either way — this only changes what\nTypeScript will let you write. `ChatStream` is the right default for reading\nTanStack AI's own events with full type safety; fall back to `StreamChunk`\nfor the branches that read your own.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Event metadata](./metadata) — `metadata.tanstack` fields a custom AG-UI server must send so `useChat` gets `finishReason` and model.\n- [Sandbox Events](../sandbox/events) — the sandbox- and harness-specific rows of this table, in context, plus `sandbox.file.diff`'s opt-in.\n- [Observability](../sandbox/observability) — the server-side hook accessors (`before()`/`after()`/`diff()`) that back `sandbox.file.diff`.\n- [Showing Code Mode in the UI](../code-mode/client-integration) — rendering the `code_mode:*` events live.\n- [Streaming UIs](../structured-outputs/streaming) — reading `structured-output.complete` end to end.\n- [Stream Events](../chat/stream-events) for the standard AG-UI `StreamChunk` lifecycle this union extends.\n"}
